# Copy to stack/.env on the VPS and fill in. stack/.env is gitignored.
#
# Every path must be a LITERAL ABSOLUTE PATH. Do not use `$HOME` or `~`.
#
# `${HOME}` resolves from the environment of whatever process invokes docker
# compose. From your shell it works; from cron or a systemd unit, where HOME is
# usually unset, it expands to an EMPTY STRING and yields a path like
# `/spa-api/nginx/conf` with no error. A literal `~` is never expanded at all
# and is treated as a relative path segment.
#
# Both failures are silent, and docker compounds them: a missing bind-mount
# source is created as an empty directory instead of failing. An empty conf
# directory means nginx starts and serves nothing.
#
# Verify before starting the stack:
#   ls -d "$NGINX_CONF_DIR" "$SNIPPETS_DIR" "$CERTS_ROOT/conf" "$CERTS_ROOT/www"

# --- nginx config, written by `vpsctl apply` --------------------------------
# Round one points these at the spa-api checkout, which is where the running
# nginx already reads them from. Moving them is a round-two step, kept separate
# so that taking over the containers does not also move the certificates.
NGINX_CONF_DIR=/root/spa-api/nginx/conf
SNIPPETS_DIR=/root/spa-api/nginx/snippets

# --- Let's Encrypt state ----------------------------------------------------
# Contains conf/ (mounted as /etc/letsencrypt) and www/ (the ACME webroot).
# Losing this directory means reissuing every certificate. Back it up before
# any cutover, and copy the backup off the host.
CERTS_ROOT=/root/spa-api/certbot

# --- nginx access/error logs ------------------------------------------------
# New in this repo. Must exist before the stack starts.
NGINX_LOG_DIR=/root/spa-api/nginx/log

# --- Netdata ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Display name for this host in the dashboard. Cosmetic.
MONITOR_HOSTNAME=balispacafe-vps

# --- ACME registration ------------------------------------------------------
# Read by `vpsctl cert issue` via apps.yml. Expiry notices go here.
ACME_EMAIL=dangkhoaddk12@gmail.com
